ine/godot/issues/117486","id":4076713177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7y_bTZ","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T17:27:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T17:27:25Z","body":"> It sounds like \"Always\" and \"Control Supports Keyboard Input\" should be doing the same thing, as these buttons are controlled via keyboard inputs.\n\nBy \"Keyboard Input\", it means `Control` nodes that take text input, such as `LineEdit`. Not the most intuitively named setting, I admit.\n\n> Where is the focus going to? I can lose focus by clicking away, but obviously can't regain it via the same clicking since the buttons are ignoring mouse actions.\n\nThe focus is not being lost be begin with. The setting only affects the visual representation of focus.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076713177/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4077962161","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117486#issuecomment-4077962161","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117486","id":4077962161,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zEMOx","user":{"login":"SpandexEnthusiast","id":268720000,"node_id":"U_kgDOEARXgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268720000?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast","html_url":"https://github.com/SpandexEnthusiast","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T20:56:40Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T20:56:40Z","body":"If the focus isn't being lost, it feels like the visual representation of the focus changing is a bug then. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4077962161/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4078212747","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117486#issuecomment-4078212747","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117486","id":4078212747,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zFJaL","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T21:52:37Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T21:53:18Z","body":"Not really, it's similar to how it works in a browser. If you focus an element with <kbd>Shift</kbd> and then click somewhere else, that focus disappears.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4078212747/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4078486071","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117486#issuecomment-4078486071","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117486","id":4078486071,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zGMI3","user":{"login":"SpandexEnthusiast","id":268720000,"node_id":"U_kgDOEARXgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268720000?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast","html_url":"https://github.com/SpandexEnthusiast","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T22:53:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T22:54:08Z","body":"> Not really, it's similar to how it works in a browser. If you focus an element with Shift and then click somewhere else, that focus disappears.\n\nI understand that, but Godot is a game engine, not a browser.   \n\nIf we always want **something** to be in focus, with focus only changing to another focusable button, what is the expectation?  As it exists now, we haven't lost focus, but look like we have.  If I press confirm, I still interact with the object that has seemingly lost focus. \n\nThat definitely seems like a visual bug.  If I shift-arrow around a browser window and focus on something, and then click away and press enter, I do not interact with the thing that was previously highlighted orange. \n\nConsider something like a cursor driven menu that has nothing to do with the mouse pointer or clicks.  The clicking now interferes with that design.\n\nHow can the mouse in general just be disabled?    Is the \"always\" option previously mentioned the only option?\n\nFWIW, Unity had this exact same problem years ago with the only real solution being to sandbag your currently focused item, trap the mouse clicks, and reset the focus.  It always created a visual blip in the process, and was generally unacceptable.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4078486071/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4079263398","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117486#issuecomment-4079263398","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117486","id":4079263398,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zJJ6m","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T02:48:40Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T02:48:40Z","body":"> How can the mouse in general just be disabled? Is the \"always\" option previously mentioned the only option?\n\nYes. Switching to that options make it behave exactly like it was pre-4.6.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4079263398/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4082633271","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117486#issuecomment-4082633271","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117486","id":4082633271,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zWAo3","user":{"login":"SpandexEnthusiast","id":268720000,"node_id":"U_kgDOEARXgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/268720000?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast","html_url":"https://github.com/SpandexEnthusiast","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpandexEnthusiast/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T13:37:49Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T13:37:49Z","body":"> > How can the mouse in general just be disabled? Is the \"always\" option previously mentioned the only option?\n> \n> Yes. Switching to that options make it behave exactly like it was pre-4.6.\n\nOK.  I think maybe the documentation surrounding it could be clearer, but regardless, I think the new change is a bit wrong.\n\nYou either need to only allow focus to go away when another focusable object is clicked on, or make sure the focus AND the visual representation of the focus are both cleared when clicking off of the item.\n\nRight now it is visually misleading and doesn't function like your browser example, or something like File Explorer. \n\nIf you keyboard navigate around the File Explorer on Windows, focus only changes to things that can be interacted with.  Dead space like the menu bar area that has no options doesn't remove focus if you click on it.  \n\nThis change seems to conflate the idea of like \"selected\" and \"focused\" , like if you click an icon in File Explorer and highlight it, but then click the dead space in the folder, the icon continues to have a light dotted box around it. \n\nThe full highlight goes away.  You can't interact again until you regrab focus.  Pressing space regrabs focus, and then you can press enter again to interact with the icon (and open the file or whatever you were highlighting).\n\nRight now in Godot's case, I am able to interact with something that is not visually focused.  That doesn't seem like correct behavior for UI elements.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4082633271/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4422251511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117486#issuecomment-4422251511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117486","id":4422251511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABB5Yz9w","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-11T15:42:25Z","updated_at":"2026-05-11T15:42:25Z","body":"Closing this, as the \"problem\" has been addressed with #115782. However, the points surrounding documentation and intent stand; you're welcome to make a proposal revolving around that!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4422251511/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]